# Build output
build/

# Sony Camera Remote SDK.
#
# The shared libraries are NOT committed - they are large, they are pure binary,
# and `make sdk` stages them from your own copy of the official package.
lib/
#
# The CRSDK *headers* ARE committed, deliberately. They are the only authoritative
# source for property codes, enum values and their semantics, and reading them is
# what distinguishes a real diagnosis from a guess - three separate faults on
# 2026-08-16 were only explained by going to these headers (a 1-based caution enum
# misread as a bitmask, an unread overheating property, an unread card-writing
# state). Vendoring them costs 288 KB and saves hours.
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PRIVATE AND MUST STAY PRIVATE while these are in it: the SDK
# is proprietary and licensed to us, not ours to publish. If this repo is ever made
# public, strip include/CRSDK/ from the history first.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Runtime state (rigd writes these outside the repo, but be explicit)
*.jsonl
.DS_Store

# Claude Code session/tooling state
.claude/

# Vendor documentation trees (1.5 GB, keep local only)
docs/basler-frame-grabber-documentation-v29-en/
docs/basler-product-documentation-v133-en/

# Linux aarch64 SDK staged for the Pi nodes (make sdk-linux). Same reason as
# lib/: large, binary, proprietary, and staged from your own copy.
lib-linux/
